{
  "requirement": "Under {cite}`requirements.cli.skill_structure`, the `habeas` skill MUST be the home of routing tasks to skills, `habeas status` and `habeas info`, directive and reference syntax, distributed requirements, and gotchas common to every task.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject requires the `habeas` skill to be the home of five topics: routing tasks to skills, `habeas status` and `habeas info`, directive and reference syntax, distributed requirements, and common gotchas. The cited `requirements.cli.skill_structure` adds that a topic is stated in full in exactly one skill, its home. The only marked test is `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_habeas_skill_is_home_of_routing_inspection_syntax_and_shared_gotchas]`.\n\nI mapped each obligation to an assertion:\n- **Routing:** the `## Workflow` section of `habeas` must contain the `| Task | Skill |` table.\n- **`habeas status` and `habeas info`:** the `## Inspecting` section must contain both command forms, `habeas status [<selection>]` and `habeas info <selection>`.\n- **Directive syntax:** the `## Requirements, examples, and definitions` section must describe the `{req}`, `{example}` and `{definition}` directives.\n- **Reference syntax:** the `## References` section must contain the full-name comment form and the fenced form.\n- **Distributed requirements:** `references/distributed-requirements.md` must exist in the `habeas` skill and carry the `# Distributed requirements` heading. `references/syntax-details.md` must contain the `## Full names in nested chapters` and `## Anchors` headings.\n- **Gotchas:** the `## Gotchas` section must contain the working-directory discovery gotcha.\n- **Exactly one home:** `assert_home(\"habeas\")` uses `home_markers`. First, it asserts that the `habeas` skill, including its references, contains every marker phrase. The markers cover the routing table, selection and glob semantics, full names, fenced references, violations and site queries, silent no-definition and nested-fence gotchas, target artifacts, and install prerequisites. Second, it asserts that none of the other four skills in `SKILLS` contains any of those phrases. This covers the cited rule that each topic is stated in exactly one skill.\n\nThe helpers `section`, `assert_text`, `skill_md`, `skill_file`, `bundled_skill` and `collapse` do real checks. `section` extracts the body up to the next heading of the same or higher level and ignores code fences. `assert_text` fails if a phrase is missing. `skill_files` uses `include_str!` on the bundled skill files, so the test reads the shipped skill text.\n\nThe test covers every named topic with a presence assertion and a non-restatement check. I found no requirement-violating behavior it would accept. I did not read the skill text in full, because its paragraph contents were not returned to me. I judged only that the assertions would fail if the topics moved or were duplicated.",
  "references": "3e613787d62d50092286fd528020c2381ceb86235c44291883f55c4a6d9690e7",
